--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4b130f89e5db22c4ebaf3dedcdb8e85b, type: 3}
  m_Name: BossDialogueDatabase
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueDatabase
  dialogues:
  - questID: RepairFenceQuest
    introLines:
    - "You're back just in time, partner. The animals have been acting strange lately
      \u2014 restless at night, pacing the fence line..."
    - "Every morning I find more boards torn loose, like something big leaned against
      them\u2026 or tried to climb over."
    - "I can\u2019t tell if it\u2019s the wind, or if they\u2019re being spooked
      by something out there in the dark."
    - "If you\u2019ve got the hands for it, I need that fence mended before we lose
      the whole herd."
    activeLines:
    - "The animals were uneasy again last night. You feel that chill in the air?
      Something\u2019s not right."
    - "I keep hearing the posts creak after midnight, like something\u2019s pushing
      on them\u2026 slow and heavy."
    - "Stay sharp out there while you\u2019re working. If you hear breathing \u2014
      don\u2019t look toward the trees."
    completeLines:
    - "You fixed it, then? That\u2019s a relief\u2026 though I could swear the air\u2019s
      heavier now that it\u2019s done."
    - "Funny thing \u2014 the animals are quiet tonight. Too quiet."
    - "If you see anything out there beyond the fence line, don\u2019t try to be
      a hero. Just come running."
  - questID: SpendAtShopQuest
    introLines:
    - "You\u2019ve earned a break after all that work, kid."
    - "Why don\u2019t you head over to the shop on the far side of the ranch?"
    - "Pick up a can of Red Bull and a pack of cigarettes. Trust me, they\u2019ll
      come in handy."
    - "They\u2019re not just for show either. Both will help patch you up when you\u2019re
      hurt.  "
    activeLines:
    - "Don\u2019t tell me you\u2019re still standing here empty-handed."
    - "Head over to the shop. It\u2019s on the far side of the ranch just behind
      us."
    - "Buy yourself that Red Bull and pack of cigarettes. You\u2019ll see how they
      work soon enough."
    completeLines:
    - "Got your Red Bull and smokes? Good. You\u2019ll need them."
    - The Red Bull will give you a quick kick. You can drink it by pressing 1. Heals
      you up in a flash, but not by much.
    - The cigarettes are a little different. Pop one in your mouth and every puff
      gives a short, sharp bit of healing. You can use them by pressing 2.
    - "You\u2019ll get more health out of a cigarette overall, and you can keep one
      lit to heal faster while you move."
    - "Don\u2019t overdo it though. That\u2019s advice for both healing and life."
  - questID: ShootCowsQuest
    introLines:
    - "Alright\u2026 we\u2019ve got a new problem. And it\u2019s shaped like a giant,
      angry steak on legs."
    - The cows have gone feral. Red eyes, foam, the whole nightmare package.
    - "I don\u2019t know what spooked them, but they\u2019re charging at anything
      that moves."
    - Take this gun and put down a few before they trample the whole farm!
    activeLines:
    - I can still hear their angry mooing echoing across the fields.
    - You sure you counted right? Pretty sure a few are still stomping around.
    - "Go on. Give \u2018em another surprise."
    completeLines:
    - "Wow\u2026 you actually did it."
    - "I saw dust clouds, heard gunshots, and then\u2026 silence. Beautiful silence."
    - You handled those cows like a seasoned hunter.
    - "Take your reward. You\u2019ve earned it. Keep the gun too."
  allQuestsCompleteLines:
  - "You\u2019ve done everything I asked, and the ranch looks whole again\u2026 but
    some nights I still hear them."
  - "It\u2019s not the animals. It\u2019s deeper than that. The kind of sound you
    feel in your ribs."
  - "Keep your eyes open out there, partner. Fences don\u2019t stop what comes crawling
    under."
